and other facilities for the development of teaching and research andtechnological development as the Board may, on the recommendation ofAcademic Council, determine;vii. make provisions for teaching, training, research, service to communrty andfor the application, advancement and dissemination of knowledge in suchmanner as it may determine;viii. decide teaching methods and sffategies to provide for effective educational
and training programs;hold examinations in the prescribed manner and, if a person qualifies theexamination, award degree, diploma, certificate and other academicdistinction to the person;provide for such instruction for persons not being students of theUniversity as it may prescribe, and to grant certificates and diplomas tosuch persons;confer degree on a person who has successfully conducted research in theprescribed manner;award, in the prescribed manner, an honorary degree to such a person asthe Patron, on the recommendations of the Board, may approve;prescribe the terms and conditions of employment of the officers, teachersand other employees of the University;create posts in connection with teaching, research, development oftechnology, administration, and for any other purpose related thereto andto make appointments in the prescribed manner;institute University Professorship, Associate Professorship, AssistantProfessorship and Lectureship or any other post and to appoint personsthereto;engage, where necessary, a person on contract for a specified duration andspeciff the terms of the engagement;provide for and support the continuous professional development of thefaculty of the University;award financial assistance to students in need, fellowships, scholarships,bursaries, medals and prizes in the prescribed manner;provide for the residence of the students, establish and maintain halls ofresidence and may approve or license a hostel, lodging or boarding place;promote the co-curricular and recreational activities of the students and tomake arrangements for promotion of health and general welfare of thestudents;take disciplinary action agains! and impose penalty on, students in theprescribed manner;demand and receive such fees and other charges from the students as itmay determine;provide career counseling and job-search services to the students andalumni;maintain linkages with alumni;maintain order, discipline and security in campuses of the University andthe constituent colleges and constituent institutions;develop and implement fund-raising plans;maintain effective coordination with stakeholders on the establishment andenhancement of Endowment Fund contributions for the University in theprescribed manner;

