8. cers of t e iversi .- The following shall be the Officers of theUniversity:(a) Patron;(b) Chairman;(c) Rector;(d) Pro-Rector;(e) Deans;(0 Chairpersons;(g) Registrar;(h) Treasurer;(i) Controller of Examinations;(a) Director, Quality Enhancement Cell;C) Director, Office of Research, Innovation and Commercialization;(k) Librarian;and0) such other persons as may be prescribed by Regulations to be theOfficers of the University.
9. Patron.{l) The Patron or his nominee shall preside over a convocationofthe University.
(2) The University may confer an honorary degree with the prior approval ofthe Patron.
1 . s ectio a d i.y.{l) The Patron may cause inspection or inquiryinto the affairs of the University.(2) The Patron shall convey his views with regard to the result of inspection orinquiry to the Board and may, after ascertaining the views of the Board, recommendany remedial action to the Board.(3) The Board shall, within the time specified by the Patron, submit a report tothe Patron about the action taken on the recommendations of the Patron'
(4) If the Board fails to take action to the satisfaction of the Patron within thespecified time, the Patron may issue such directions as he thinks fit and the Boardshall comply with all such directions.

