. ea .-{1) There shall be a Dean of each Faculty or a group of Faculties,as may be prescribed by ih",q."t, Rules or Regulations, who shall be the Convener of theBoard of Faculty constituted in such manner as may be prescribed by the Act, Rules orRegulations.@ The Dean of each Faculty or a group of Faculties shall be appointed by theoard from amongst the three senior most Professors in the Faculty or a group ofFaculties, as the case may be, for such period as may be prescribed by the Board, andshall be eligible for re-appointment:Provided that if no Professor is available in a Faoulty, a Professor from some otherFaculty may act as a Dean till a Professor of the Faculty itself is appointed.(3) The Dean shall present candidates for admission to degree, excepthonorary degrees, in the courses falling within the purview of the Faculty.(4) The Dean shall exercise such other administrative and academic powersand perform such other functions as may be prescribed by Reguldions.
7. ir erso .-(1) The Chairperson of a teaching or research departmenlPrincipal of a constituent college/institute or Director of a constituent college/instituteshall be appointed by the Board on the recommendation of the Rector.(2) The Chairperson of a teaohing or research departrnent, Principal of a constituentcollege/institute or Director of a constituent college/institute shall be appointed fromamongst the three senior most Professors of a teaching or research department,constituent college or constituent institute for such period as may prescribed by theBoar{ and shall be eligible for re-appointment but if, in a teaching or researchdepartmen! constituent college or constituent institute, no hofessor is available, theappointment shall be made from amongst the three senior most Associate Professors of ateaching or research departmen! constituent college or constituent institute:Provided that in a teaching or research department, constituent college orconstituent instifute, where there is no Professor or Associate Professor is available, nosuch appointnent shall be made and a teaching or research department, constituentcollege or constituent institute shall be looked after by the Dean of the Faculty with theassistance of the senior most teacher of a teaching or research department, constifuentcollege or constifuent institute.(3) The Chairperson shall plan, organue and supervise the work of a teachingor research department, constituent college or constituent instifute, as the case may be,and shall be responsible to the Dean for the work assigned to him.. egistrar.-(1) The Board shall appoint a Registrar of the university.(2) The experience, professional and academic qualifications necessary forappointment to the post of Registrar, method and manner of appointnent as well as termsand conditions of appointment shall be as may be prescribed by Regulations.

