subject approvod by the Board on the recommendation of the Selection Board.- (6i The Board may revise the standing list of experts of a subject on therecommendation of the Selection Board.
. ctio s of t e Selectio oar .- The Selection Board shall:
(a) consider the applications and recommend to the Board, the names ofsuitable candidates for appoinfinent to teaching and other posts andrecommend suitable salary for the selected candidate;(b) consider all cases of promotion of officers of the University andrecommend the names of suitable candidates for such promotion to theBoard; and(c) consider all cases of honorari4 allowances, incentives for teaching andother posts and submit specific recommendations to the Board for itsconsideration.
. i ance a ^ i g Co ittee.-{t) The Finance and PlanningCommittee shall consist of:(a) Rector (Convener);(b) All the Deans;(c) One nominee of the Company;(d) One member of the Board to be nominated by the Board;(e) Director Planning of the Commission;(f) Director, Office of Research, Innovation and Commercialization;(g) Registrar;and(h) Treasurer (Secretary)(2) e members other than ex officio members of the Finance and PlanningCommittee shall hold office for a term of three years and shall be eligible for re-appointment on the expiry of their term of office.(3) Four members of the Finance and Planning Cornmittee shall constitute thequorum for a meeting ofthe Finance and Planning Committee.42. ctio soft e i a cea an i gCo ittee.--TheFinanceandPlanning Committee shall:(a) prepare the annual statement of accounts and propose annual budgetestimates and advise the Board thereon;(b) review periodically the furancial position of the University;(c) advise the Board on all matters relating to fee structure, finance,investments and accounts of the University; and(d) perform such other functions as may be prescribed by the Regulations.3. isci i e Co ittee.{l) The Discipline Committee shall consist of:
(a) the Convener to be nominated by the Rector;(b) two Professors to be nominated by the Board;(c) two Associate Professors to be nominated by the Academic Council; and(d) the teacher or officer-in-charge of students' affairs, by whatever name

