7.2
called (Member/Secretary).(2) The members other than ex-officio members of the Discipline Committee shall holdoffice for a term of three years and shall be eligible for re-appointment on the expiry of theirterm of offrce.
(3) The quorum for a meeting of the Discipline Committee shall be four
members.
4. ctio s o t e isci li e o ittee.-The functions of theDiscipline Committee shall be to:(a) propose Regulations to the Academic Council relating to the oonduct ofUniversity students, maintenance of discipline and breach of discipline;and(b) perform such other functions as may be prescribed.45. Apoit etof Co ittees ycertainAtorities.{l)TheBoard, the Academic Council and other Authorities may, from time to timq appoint suchstanding, special or advisory c,ommittees, as they may deem fit, and may place on suchcommittee persons who are not members of the Authorities appointing the Committees.(2) The constitution, functions and powers of the Authorities for whichno specific provision has been made in this Act shall be such as may be prescribed byRegulations.
CVA}[CA VS NS6. iversi d.-{1) The Board shall establish a Fund to beknown as 'fhe Margalla Intemational University Fund which shall vest in theUniversity and to which shall be credited all sums received by the University-(2) The University may accept donations in the shape of money, land,vehicles, equipment or any other item that may facilitate the functioning of theUniversity and all such donations shall be used, maintained and disposed of by theUniversity in the prescribed manner.
7, get, A it a Acco ts.{l) The budget of the Universityshall be approved and its accounts shall be maintained and audited in such manner asmay be determined by the Board.(2) The Board may approve the budget of the University, appropriationsof accounts of the University and settle an audit para relating to the audit of theUniversity.

