51. les.{l) The Authorities and the other bodies of the Universitymay make Rules, to be published in the University's Gazette, consistent with the Act,Statutes or the Regulations, to regulate any matter relating to the affairs of the Universitywhioh has not been provided for by the Act or that is not required to be regulated byStatutes or Regulations, including rules to regulate the conduct of business and the timeand place of meetings and related matters.(2) Rules shall become effective upon approval by the Board ofGovemors.
C
52. pport ni to s ow ca se.-Except as otherwise provided bylaw no officer, teacher or other employee of the University holding a permanent post shallbe reduced in ranlg or removed or compulsorily retired from service for cause arising outof any act or omission on the part of the person concerned unless he has been given areasonable opportunity of showing cause against the action proposed to be taken.53. Appeal to t e xec tive Co ittee and t e oar ofover ors.-Where an order is passed punishing any officer (other than the Chairmanand Rector), teacher or other employee of the University or altering or interpreting to hisdisadvantage the prescribed terms or conditions of his service, he/she shall, where theorder is passed by any officer or teacher of the University other than the Chairman andRector, have the right to appeal to the Executive Committee against the order, and wherethe order is passed by the Chairman or Rector, have the right to appeal to the Board ofGovernors.
S . ene ts a s ra ce.{l) The University shall constitute forthe benefit of its officers, teachers and other employees schemes, as may be prescribed,for the provision of post-employment benefits as well as health and life insurance while inservice.
55. e oval of i c lties. -{1) If any question arises as to theinterpretation of any of the provisions of the Act, it shall be placed before the Patron andHigher, Education Commission (HEC) whose decision thereon shall be final'(2) If any difficulty arises in giving effect to any of the provisions of theAct, the Patron may make such order after obtaining the views of the Board ofGovernors, not inconsistent with the provisions of the Act, as may appear to him to benecessary for removing the difficulty.(3) Where the Act makes any provision for anything to be done but noprovision or no sufficient provision has been made as respects the authority by whom, orihe time at which, or the manner in which, it shall be done, then it shall be done by suchauthority, at such time, or in such manner as the Patron may direct after obtaining theviews of the Board ofGovernors.
56. e i .-No suit or legal proceedings shall lie against the

